    </a>
    <button data-dc-tpl="44" class="scp4" style="padding: 10px 16px; background: var(--action); color: var(--action-ink); border: 0px; border-radius: 9px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; flex-shrink: 0; white-space: nowrap;">Check my domain</button>
  </div></header><main data-dc-tpl="386" style="max-width: 1240px; margin: 0px auto; padding: clamp(56px, 6vw, 80px) clamp(16px, 3vw, 32px) 110px;">
  <div data-dc-tpl="387" style="max-width: 680px; margin-bottom: 64px;">
    <div data-dc-tpl="388" style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.2em; color: var(--action); margin-bottom: 16px;">PLATFORM</div>
    <h1 data-dc-tpl="389" style="font-size: clamp(36px, 4.6vw, 52px); line-height: 1.06; letter-spacing: -0.03em; font-weight: 800; margin: 0px 0px 18px; text-wrap: balance;">Six signal families, one readable score.</h1>
    <p data-dc-tpl="390" style="font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); margin: 0px; text-wrap: pretty;">HIP does not guess at intent. It measures things that can be checked, weights them with rules anyone can read, and shows the arithmetic.</p>
  </div>

  <div data-dc-tpl="391" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(340px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-bottom: 80px;">
    <div data-dc-tpl="392" style="background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 18px; padding: 32px;">
      <div data-dc-tpl="393" style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;"><span data-dc-tpl="394" style="font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--action);">01</span><h3 data-dc-tpl="395" style="font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Transport &amp; certificates</h3></div>
      <p data-dc-tpl="396" style="font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--muted); margin: 0px 0px 18px;">Does the site force HTTPS? Are redirects clean? Is the certificate valid, from a trusted issuer, and not about to expire? Weak transport is the most common fixable problem HIP finds.</p>
      <div data-dc-tpl="397" style="display: flex; gap: 7px; flex-wrap: wrap;"><span data-dc-tpl="398" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">https.enforced</span><span data-dc-tpl="399" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">tls.version</span><span data-dc-tpl="400" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">cert.expiry</span></div>
    </div>
    <div data-dc-tpl="401" style="background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 18px; padding: 32px;">
      <div data-dc-tpl="402" style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;"><span data-dc-tpl="403" style="font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--action);">02</span><h3 data-dc-tpl="404" style="font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">DNS &amp; ownership</h3></div>
      <p data-dc-tpl="405" style="font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--muted); margin: 0px 0px 18px;">Record configuration, mail-authentication posture, and a TXT-record proof that ties a domain to the person managing it. Verification is what separates a scan from a claim.</p>
      <div data-dc-tpl="406" style="display: flex; gap: 7px; flex-wrap: wrap;"><span data-dc-tpl="407" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">dns.records</span><span data-dc-tpl="408" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">mail.auth</span><span data-dc-tpl="409" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">owner.txt</span></div>
    </div>
    <div data-dc-tpl="410" style="background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 18px; padding: 32px;">
      <div data-dc-tpl="411" style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;"><span data-dc-tpl="412" style="font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--action);">03</span><h3 data-dc-tpl="413" style="font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Domain reputation</h3></div>
      <p data-dc-tpl="414" style="font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--muted); margin: 0px 0px 18px;">Age, history, hosting context and third-party listings. A brand-new domain is not automatically bad — but it carries less evidence, and the score says so out loud.</p>
      <div data-dc-tpl="415" style="display: flex; gap: 7px; flex-wrap: wrap;"><span data-dc-tpl="416" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">domain.age</span><span data-dc-tpl="417" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">listings</span></div>
    </div>
    <div data-dc-tpl="418" style="background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 18px; padding: 32px;">
      <div data-dc-tpl="419" style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;"><span data-dc-tpl="420" style="font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--action);">04</span><h3 data-dc-tpl="421" style="font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Page behaviour</h3></div>
      <p data-dc-tpl="422" style="font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--muted); margin: 0px 0px 18px;">Where forms post to, what third parties load, whether credentials are requested over insecure channels, and whether the page tries to obscure what it is doing.</p>
      <div data-dc-tpl="423" style="display: flex; gap: 7px; flex-wrap: wrap;"><span data-dc-tpl="424" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">form.targets</span><span data-dc-tpl="425" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">third.party</span><span data-dc-tpl="426" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">obfuscation</span></div>
    </div>
    <div data-dc-tpl="427" style="background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 18px; padding: 32px;">
      <div data-dc-tpl="428" style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;"><span data-dc-tpl="429" style="font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--action);">05</span><h3 data-dc-tpl="430" style="font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Wording &amp; pressure patterns</h3></div>
      <p data-dc-tpl="431" style="font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--muted); margin: 0px 0px 18px;">Language that manufactures urgency, impersonates a provider, or pushes for credentials. These rules are the most contestable, so they are the most openly documented — and appealable.</p>
      <div data-dc-tpl="432" style="display: flex; gap: 7px; flex-wrap: wrap;"><span data-dc-tpl="433" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">urgency</span><span data-dc-tpl="434" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">impersonation</span></div>
    </div>
    <div data-dc-tpl="435" style="background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 18px; padding: 32px;">
      <div data-dc-tpl="436" style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;"><span data-dc-tpl="437" style="font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--action);">06</span><h3 data-dc-tpl="438" style="font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">External provider results</h3></div>
      <p data-dc-tpl="439" style="font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--muted); margin: 0px 0px 18px;">SSL Labs, Google Safe Browsing and VirusTotal feed in as attributed signals. HIP records which provider said what, and when, so a verdict can be traced to its source.</p>
      <div data-dc-tpl="440" style="display: flex; gap: 7px; flex-wrap: wrap;"><span data-dc-tpl="441" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">provider.ssllabs</span><span data-dc-tpl="442" style="padding: 5px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace;">provider.gsb</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div data-dc-tpl="443" style="background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 22px; padding: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 48px); display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(340px, 1fr)); gap: 52px; align-items: center;">
    <div data-dc-tpl="444">
      <div data-dc-tpl="445" style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.2em; color: var(--action); margin-bottom: 14px;">SCORING</div>
      <h2 data-dc-tpl="446" style="font-size: clamp(25px, 2.8vw, 32px); line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.025em; font-weight: 800; margin: 0px 0px 16px; text-wrap: balance;">Rules you can read, argue with, and change.</h2>
      <p data-dc-tpl="447" style="font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--muted); margin: 0px 0px 18px; text-wrap: pretty;">Detection rules and their weights are plain configuration in the repository. Propose a change, discuss it in the open, and see the effect on real scans before it ships.</p>
      <p data-dc-tpl="448" style="font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--muted); margin: 0px;">Every scored domain keeps an audit history: what changed, when, and which rule version produced it.</p>
    </div>
    <div data-dc-tpl="449" style="background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; padding: 22px; font-family: &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;, monospace; font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.85; overflow: auto;">
      <div data-dc-tpl="450" style="color: var(--muted);"># rules/transport.yml</div>
      <div data-dc-tpl="451"><span data-dc-tpl="452" style="color: var(--violet);">id</span><span data-dc-tpl="453" style="color: var(--muted);">:</span> https.not_enforced</div>
      <div data-dc-tpl="454"><span data-dc-tpl="455" style="color: var(--violet);">severity</span><span data-dc-tpl="456" style="color: var(--muted);">:</span> <span data-dc-tpl="457" style="color: var(--warn);">high</span></div>
      <div data-dc-tpl="458"><span data-dc-tpl="459" style="color: var(--violet);">weight</span><span data-dc-tpl="460" style="color: var(--muted);">:</span> <span data-dc-tpl="461" style="color: var(--action);">-18</span></div>
      <div data-dc-tpl="462"><span data-dc-tpl="463" style="color: var(--violet);">reason</span><span data-dc-tpl="464" style="color: var(--muted);">:</span> "This site does not force a<br data-dc-tpl="465">&nbsp;&nbsp;secure connection, so visitors can<br data-dc-tpl="466">&nbsp;&nbsp;be served over plain HTTP."</div>
      <div data-dc-tpl="467"><span data-dc-tpl="468" style="color: var(--violet);">fix</span><span data-dc-tpl="469" style="color: var(--muted);">:</span> "Redirect all HTTP traffic to<br data-dc-tpl="470">&nbsp;&nbsp;HTTPS and enable HSTS."</div>
      <div data-dc-tpl="471"><span data-dc-tpl="472" style="color: var(--violet);">appealable</span><span data-dc-tpl="473" style="color: var(--muted);">:</span> <span data-dc-tpl="474" style="color: var(--ok);">true</span></div>
    </div>
  </div></main><footer data-dc-tpl="667" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--surface);">
  <div data-dc-tpl="668" style="max-width: 1240px; margin: 0px auto; padding: 56px 32px 40px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(190px, 1fr)); gap: 40px;">
    <div data-dc-tpl="669">
      <div data-dc-tpl="670" style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 11px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
        <img data-dc-tpl="671" src="/images/public/reference/hip-shield.png" alt="HIP" style="height: 42px; width: auto; display: block; flex-shrink: 0;">
        <div data-dc-tpl="672" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; line-height: 1;">
          <span data-dc-tpl="673" style="font-size: 21px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--text); white-space: nowrap;">HIP</span>
          <span data-dc-tpl="674" style="font-size: 9.5px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 5px; white-space: nowrap;">Human-Interactive Protocol</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p data-dc-tpl="675" style="font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--muted); margin: 0px; max-width: 280px;">An open trust and risk layer for websites and online content. Community-built, evidence-first.</p>
    </div>
    <div data-dc-tpl="676" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 11px;">
      <div data-dc-tpl="677" style="font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 3px;">PRODUCT</div>
      <button data-dc-tpl="678" class="scp7" style="background: none; border: 0px; padding: 0px; text-align: left; font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--text); cursor: pointer;">Platform</button>
      <button data-dc-tpl="679" class="scp7" style="background: none; border: 0px; padding: 0px; text-align: left; font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--text); cursor: pointer;">How it works</button>
      <button data-dc-tpl="680" class="scp7" style="background: none; border: 0px; padding: 0px; text-align: left; font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--text); cursor: pointer;">Verification</button>
      <button data-dc-tpl="681" class="scp7" style="background: none; border: 0px; padding: 0px; text-align: left; font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--text); cursor: pointer;">Developers</button>
    </div>
    <div data-dc-tpl="682" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 11px;">
      <div data-dc-tpl="683" style="font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 3px;">OPEN SOURCE</div>
      <a data-dc-tpl="684" href="https://github.com/daCodez/HIP" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="scp7" style="font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--text);">Repository</a>
      <a data-dc-tpl="685" href="https://github.com/daCodez/HIP" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="scp7" style="font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--text);">Detection rules</a>
      <a data-dc-tpl="686" href="https://github.com/daCodez/HIP" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="scp7" style="font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--text);">Contributing</a>
      <a data-dc-tpl="687" href="https://github.com/daCodez/HIP" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="scp7" style="font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--text);">Issues</a>
